.TITLE "tar"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manipulates file archives. It is used to __combine multiple files__ into a single archive file, often referred to as a tarball, for storage or distribution.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**tar -c -v -f archive.tar folder**
Creates a new archive from the contents of a specified directory.
> __-c__ create flag | __-v__ verbose flag | __-f__ file flag | __archive.tar__ target archive name | __folder__ source directory

**tar -x -v -f archive.tar**
Extracts the contents of an archive into the current directory.
> __-x__ extract flag

**tar -z -c -v -f archive.tar.gz folder**
Creates a compressed archive using gzip.
> __-z__ gzip compression flag

**tar -t -f archive.tar**
Lists the contents of an archive without extracting them.
> __-t__ list flag

**tar -j -c -v -f archive.tar.bz2 folder**
Creates a compressed archive using bzip2.
> __-j__ bzip2 compression flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
On macOS, the __tar__ utility is the BSD version and handles Apple-specific metadata like extended attributes. Using the __-v__ flag is helpful for monitoring progress when archiving large numbers of files.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:zip** **mac:gzip**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/tar.html__
